      "writtenOn": "2025-07-16T15:22:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is this being introduced? It is almost always incorrect to call this since it is information destroying. The user can `font-\u003egetPath(gid).value_or(SkPath())` if they really want this behavior.",
      "revId": "4e437bc3dac3a63086d4a79d84ddd67566988a42",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8305a18b_1ae866d8",
        "filename": "include/core/SkFont.h",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 445,
      "author": {
        "id": 5648
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-07-16T15:59:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Well, nearly every call site doesn\u0027t care about the distinction, as they treat empty and not representable as the same thing. Hence the helper to simplify so many callers.\n\nThat said, I had forgotton about value_or() as a pattern for the existing callsites. I will switch to that.\n\nWhile were on this topic, given the desire to make it clear that \u0027getPath\u0027 may fail, we\u0027re in a position to give it a different name if you like?\n- asPath(), glyphAsPath(), getIfPath(), etc.\n\nDo you have any preferred name, or should I use getPath() for the optional one?",
      "parentUuid": "4fd4ae44_75176ee3",
      "revId": "4e437bc3dac3a63086d4a79d84ddd67566988a42",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
